% Lesson 2 - Hyperedges: from terms to a graph.
%
% cArg derives C from TWO open sites (A and B) through the axiom abc.
% That single subargument is one hyperedge with two sources - the reason
% edges are poly-arrows rather than binary.
%
% bArg then supports the B site strictly, adding a second edge.
lk.
declare A,B,C:bool.
declare abc : (A->(B->C)).
declare axB : (B).

start argument cArg C
cut (A->(B->C)) r.
axiom abc.
elim.
next.
elim.
next.
axiom r.
end argument

start argument bArg B
axiom axB.
end argument

debate pro open d2 : C.
cArg.
support bArg cArg.
hora est.

graph d2 show
